  "body": "## What changed\n\n`crates/app/tests/import_step_thread.rs`: remove the line `drop(point);`.\n\n`point` is a closure that borrows `ent` mutably. It has no `Drop` implementation, so `drop(point)` does nothing. Clippy 0.1.98 refuses the call with `clippy::drop_non_drop`, and `-D warnings` makes the clippy step red. The borrow ends at the last call of the closure, so the next closure can borrow `out` without the line.\n\n## Readings\n\nToolchain: rustc 1.98.0, clippy 0.1.98.\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test import_step_thread -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test import_step_thread`: 1 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`a_four_turn_thread_flank_meshes_at_full_fidelity_in_a_bounded_count` (the only test in the binary). The change is in test code only.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full clippy run of the workspace. Only the touched test binary.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff changes one test file and no product code.\n\nThe branch merges cleanly with `upstream/main` (checked with `git merge-tree`).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2794\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
